# This folder stores this component's own security-relevant scan data --
# attack-log.php, ip-list.php, login-attempts.php, geoip-cache.php,
# false-positives.php, scan-history.php -- meant to be read only by this
# extension's own PHP code (via JPATH_ADMINISTRATOR), never served
# directly over HTTP. index.html alone (still present, kept for defence
# in depth on servers that ignore this file) only stops directory
# LISTING; it does nothing to stop a direct request for a known filename.
# Denies everything here unconditionally, both the modern (Apache 2.4+)
# and legacy (2.2) syntax so this works regardless of which the host is
# still running.
#
# IMPORTANT: this .htaccess is Apache-only. nginx, Caddy/FrankenPHP,
# LiteSpeed running in its nginx-compatible mode, and IIS all ignore it
# completely, and on those a plain .json file here would have been
# readable, unauthenticated, by anyone who requested it directly. The
# *.php extension and the executable PHP stub every one of these files
# starts with (see MuruguardHelper::dataFileStubPrefix()) is the real,
# server-agnostic protection -- requesting any of them directly executes
# that stub and returns a plain 403, on literally any server capable of
# running Joomla at all. This .htaccess is defence in depth on top of
# that, not the primary protection.
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order deny,allow
    Deny from all
</IfModule>
